WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.559
Good morning John; it's Thursday, January
25th. Yesterday, you said it was Thursday;

00:00:15.559 --> 00:00:21.360
today I'm saying it's Thursday. One of us
is wrong. As you may have noticed in my January

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:26.350
23rd video, I'm currently in Mom and Dad's
little cabin on the side of their house. Katherine

00:00:26.350 --> 00:00:32.369
and I have begun our yearly Tour of the Entire
Southeastern United States!

00:00:32.369 --> 00:00:36.320
We're starting out in Asheville, North Carolina,
which is right here. Then we're going to jaunt

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:40.210
over to Athens, Georgia to see some friends,
and then jaunt back from Georgia to Asheville,

00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:45.180
and then we're going to jaunt from Asheville
to Orlando, that jaunt being in an airplane

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:50.090
- by all accounts this is a lot of jaunting
- and then we're gonna jaunt in a car from

00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:55.739
Orlando to Tampa St. Petersburg to see some
friends, and then from Tampa St. Petersburg

00:00:55.739 --> 00:01:00.680
we're going to jump to Englewood, Florida
which is pretty far down on the Gulf Coast.

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:07.700
Two of the three weeks I'll be on this trip
I'll be without high speed internet. Not okay.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:11.310
You said that you believed that Mom and Dad's
house was the last residence in the United

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:18.300
States of America with dial-up internet. You
were wrong. There's an entire town on the

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:23.320
Gulf Coast of Florida without broadband internet.
And I'm about to go there.

00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:28.970
I'm very concerned for what this means for
the Brotherhood 2.0 project. I'm also very

00:01:28.970 --> 00:01:32.380
concerned because a lot of people have been
coming up with a lot of very good punishments.

00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:35.360
These aren't the kind of punishments that
are just difficult to do, they're the kind

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:39.390
of punishments that are extremely embarrassing
to have on video blog, and that's the kind

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:41.739
of punishments that we're going to want to
be doing!

00:01:41.739 --> 00:01:45.950
So I've decided something. As the Brotherhood
2.0 brother who may be very likely be making

00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:51.810
his first foray into punishment territory,
I would like to suggest that the brother not

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:57.360
being punished decide which punishment to
give the brother being punished. That way,

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:01.270
I just don't take the punishment I'd most
want to do, but you'd give me the punishment

00:02:01.270 --> 00:02:04.239
you'd most want our viewers to see me doing.

00:02:04.239 --> 00:02:08.720
You were right about another thing about Asheville,
North Carolina. I'm surrounded by memories

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:09.720
of my childhood.

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:14.640
Do you remember when Phil Wood made us these
little critter cages so we could catch grasshoppers

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:20.990
and store them inside? So they can be punished
for the crimes of their incessant chirping!

00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:25.750
They never really worked very well.

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:30.250
This reminds me of my childhood because it
is a little dog that I made to resemble our

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:35.760
little dog, Red, and the doghouse that we
never had. He doesn't actually fit inside

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:36.760
the doghouse.

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:42.140
Oddly enough, one of the things that remind
me most of my childhood in this place is the

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:47.820
food. Mom made Shepard's Pie last night! And
also, something I haven't seen since I left

00:02:47.820 --> 00:03:00.230
home... a Kraft American cheese individually
wrapped single. It, ah, it smells like nothi-

00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:05.260
I mean, it doesn't, it's not cheese; it doesn't
look or smell like cheese, it doesn't...(laughs)

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:08.960
cheese doesn't wobble like this, holy crap!

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:14.200
There's really three ways I'd eat one of these-
on a white bread sandwich with turkey, all

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:26.430
by itself on a tortilla, microwaved, or folded
in quarters - bwaaa (laughs) - and then eat

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:27.430
it.

00:03:27.430 --> 00:03:34.450
Mmm, delicious cheese. Kinda.

00:03:34.450 --> 00:03:38.410
I enjoyed your survey, and hopefully I'll
see more of it tomorrow.

